Title: The Front Desk
Credit: original short on a common motif (a new captain doubted at her own precinct); names, events and dialogue are new
Author: Claude (draft)
Format: 8 scenes x 16 s (each scene = 2 Flow generations of 8 s, one shot each), English dialogue
Tests: a three-person set held across six scenes; a letter handled across hands (given, crumpled, binned, recovered); a desk phone call; a cut to a second location with extras
Gate1: APPROVED by Tech Lead under Owner-delegated authority 2026-11-02

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT LOBBY - MORNING

[[look: police station front lobby, tall wooden front desk on the right, grey filing cabinets on the back wall, glass entrance doors on the left, morning daylight]]

CAPTAIN NORA BELL, late forties, the precinct's new commanding officer, steps in through the glass doors in a navy wool coat. Nobody here has met her. SERGEANT WADE KESSLER, fifties, sits behind the front desk. Behind him, rookie OFFICER LUIS ORTIZ files folders at the cabinets.

KESSLER
Complaints window opens at nine.

NORA crosses to the desk and stops in front of it, calm.

NORA
I'm not here to complain.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT LOBBY - MORNING

NORA slides a folded letter across the desk. KESSLER unfolds it, reads, and looks her up and down with a thin smirk.

KESSLER
Captain? Captains here don't look like you.

KESSLER crumples the letter in one fist and drops it into the trash bin beside his chair.

KESSLER
Nice try. Next.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT LOBBY - MORNING

ORTIZ stops filing and looks from NORA to the bin, uneasy.

ORTIZ
Sarge, maybe we call upstairs?

KESSLER turns his head back toward ORTIZ without getting up.

KESSLER
Maybe you go file something.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT LOBBY - MORNING

NORA looks past KESSLER to ORTIZ, unhurried.

NORA
What's your name, officer?

ORTIZ steps to the bin, takes out the crumpled letter and smooths it flat with both hands.

ORTIZ
Ortiz, ma'am.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT LOBBY - MORNING

The desk phone rings. KESSLER lifts the receiver to his ear.

KESSLER
Desk. Yes, Lieutenant. The new captain?

ORTIZ reads from the smoothed letter, out loud.

ORTIZ
Captain Nora Bell.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT LOBBY - MORNING

NORA looks at KESSLER, level, not unkind.

NORA
Roll call is at eight, Sergeant.

KESSLER, the receiver still at his ear, swallows. The smirk is gone.

KESSLER
Yes... Captain.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT BRIEFING ROOM - MORNING

[[marker: context card "Roll call, 8 a.m."; second location, uniformed officers seated]]

NORA stands at the lectern in front of the seated officers. ORTIZ sits in the front row. KESSLER stands alone at the back wall.

NORA
We check before we judge. Every time.

NORA looks at ORTIZ.

NORA
Officer Ortiz rides with me today.

INT. EASTGATE PRECINCT BRIEFING ROOM - MORNING

ORTIZ sits up straight, surprised, and nods.

ORTIZ
Yes, ma'am.

NORA looks over the room to KESSLER at the back wall. He lowers his eyes.

NORA
Sergeant Kessler keeps the desk.
